<title>SINGAPORE: SingTel 1996/97 net profit rises 11.6 pct.</title>
<headline>SingTel 1996/97 net profit rises 11.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit (billion)		  1.66 vs   1.49</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			4.50 vs   4.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    10.88 vs   9.75</p>
<p>    Turnover (billion)		    4.42 vs   4.00</p>
<p>    Operating profit (billion)	  2.20 vs   2.05</p>
<p>    Profits/loss from associates</p>
<p>					 (gain)47.60 vs 87.80 (loss)</p>
<p>    Investment income		    48.40 vs  39.50</p>
<p>    Other income including interest  95.20 vs  82.60</p>
<p>    Tax				     585.80 vs 477.00</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (loss)  5.2  vs   0.80 (gain)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			 21.0 vs   nil</p>
<p>Note - Singapore Telecommunications Ltd is Southeast Asia's biggest telecommunications group with a total capitalisation of around Singapore $39 billion. It has a level one, sponsored American Depositary Receipt (ADR) programme for the trading of its shares in dollars.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
